<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shora Nogmov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1794–1844</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shora Nogmov was a Kabardian scholar, poet and officer in Russian service who laid foundations for the written study of the Kabardian language. He compiled a grammar and dictionary of Kabardian and wrote a History of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Adyghe</a> People based on oral traditions and songs, published after his death. He is regarded as a founder of Kabardian literature and historiography.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shora-nogmov.jpg" alt="Shora Nogmov" width="246" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KBR-Nogmov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
